messages:
oliver_sales: Maria on the PulseHealth pilot hit flaky streaming in their mobile bridge. Demo stalled — embedded bridge throws JSON.parse errors and the stream drops after ~30-50s.
neha_se: Can you upload the bridge console and any network snippets? Desktop browser works for you?
maria_pilot: Desktop is fine. The mobile bridge (custom WKWebView wrapper) fails. Console: \"Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseChunk (bridge.js:98)\". Network captured SSE data where data: lines are truncated mid-object. Posting minimal sample below.
maria_pilot: event: message
data: {"pos":3,"text":"Lead-in"}

event: message
data: {"pos":4,"text":"Continued long paragraph that gets trun

"}

The middle payload is cut and their bridge immediately calls JSON.parse on each data chunk, causing the crash.
yuri_oncall: Infra shows a short burst of 429s for that org and several upstream resets from the edge proxy at the same timeframe. Edge logs: \"recv() failed (104: Connection reset by peer)\" and proxy: \"upstream timed out (110)\". There are also proxy_buffering warnings. Could be overlap of aggressive client retries and buffer fragmentation.
neha_se: Sounds like two colliding issues: (A) the bridge assumes per-data JSON completeness and parses immediately, (B) network/proxy truncation or premature close splits JSON across frames. Short-term mitigations: instruct the bridge to buffer consecutive data: payloads and only JSON.parse when buffer forms valid JSON; ask them to disable response buffering on their CDN/proxy and increase keepalive; we can reduce gateway retry concurrency for their org to avoid retry storms.
maria_pilot: Minimal changes preferred — is there a tiny shim we can paste into the bridge JS runtime without a full rebuild? Also can you apply infra tweaks quickly?
yuri_oncall: I can apply a one-off throttle for their API key now and disable proxy_buffering for streaming routes on canary. I'll also enable periodic SSE heartbeat comments (":\n") every 12s from canary to help keep connections alive.
ci-bot: canary v2.31.5 rolled to eu-west-1 at 2141599800
neha_se: Here's a minimal, non-invasive accumulator you can inject at runtime into the bridge (paste into the console or runtime shim):
```js
// SSE accumulator - handles JSON split across data chunks without rebuild
let _acc = '';
function onBridgeSseData(dataLine) {
  // dataLine is the string extracted from the event.data payload
  _acc += dataLine;
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(_acc);
    handleStreamMessage(obj);
    _acc = '';
  } catch (err) {
    // incomplete - wait for next chunk
    if (_acc.length > 128 * 1024) { _acc = ''; console.warn('dropped oversized partial'); }
  }
}
// optional safety: flush if stuck for >5s to avoid memory growth
let _lastProgress = Date.now();
setInterval(() => { if (_acc && Date.now() - _lastProgress > 5000) { _acc = ''; } }, 5000);
```
Use this until a proper SDK patch is deployed.
maria_pilot: We'll inject the shim now and report back. Please apply the infra throttle.
yuri_oncall: Throttle applied for org pulsehealth (done). Disabled proxy_buffering on canary for streaming endpoint (done). Heartbeat comments enabled on canary (in progress). I'll also add a metric to count partial-parse failures and alert if it spikes.
neha_se: For customer guidance: avoid aggressive client-side reconnect loops for streaming endpoints — overlapping connections can cause proxy confusion and lead to truncation. We'll follow up with a small SDK helper in the JS SDK that implements robust reassembly and size/time flush policies.
oliver_sales: Thanks team. Maria, I'll coordinate and follow up prior to your exec run tomorrow. Marking as high-touch POC support. :thumbsup:
maria_pilot: Shim injected and running a smoke test now. Will report results in ~20m. Thanks for the quick turnaround.
